---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
const projects = [
  { title: 'A sauna for me & my friends', category: 'Making', percentage: 50, target: '$3,000', color: 'peach' },
  { title: 'More time for open source', category: 'Open source', percentage: 30, target: '$1,000', color: 'blue' },
  { title: 'Notes from the in-between', category: 'Writing', percentage: 20, target: '$500', color: 'green' },
];
const screens = [
  ['01', 'A home for your work', 'Projects, aspirations, and a simple way to split support.', '/demo/', 'profile'],
  ['02', 'A living project log', 'Stories, images, and updates that can travel through Bluesky.', '/demo/support/backyard-sauna/', 'story'],
  ['03', 'People worth knowing', 'Your connections, friends of friends, and recommendations.', '/demo/discover/', 'people'],
  ['04', 'The bigger picture', 'Earnings over time, project performance, and recurring support.', '/demo/studio/', 'chart'],
  ['05', 'A little social proof', 'Share what you backed with a beautiful allocation card.', '/demo/share/sample/', 'split'],
  ['06', 'Your own little studio', 'Create projects, publish updates, and manage your profile.', '/demo/studio/projects/', 'studio'],
];
---
<Site>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy"><a class="preview-pill" href="https://github.com/crs48/feedme"><span></span> Open source · early preview ↗</a><h1>Make room for<br/>what <em>matters.</em></h1><p class="hero-lead">A little support for your next project.<br/>A better sense of what your people love.</p><p class="hero-detail">Feedme lets your community tip the things they’d like to see more of. You get resources, encouragement, and a useful signal about where to put your energy. The choice is always yours.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/demo/">Explore the demo ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="/get-started/">Make it your own</a></div><p class="hero-caption">No signup to explore. No payments in the demo.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-preview" aria-label="Example of a creator support page"><div class="preview-window"><div class="preview-address"><span class="window-dots" aria-hidden="true">● ● ●</span><span>your corner of the internet</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="mini-profile"><img src="/demo/avatars/12.jpg" alt="Fictional creator Alex Rivers" width="56" height="56"/><div><strong>Alex Rivers</strong><span>@alex.example.com</span></div><span class="mini-heart" aria-hidden="true">♡</span></div><p class="mini-bio">A little code, a little sawdust,<br/>and a lot of curiosity.</p><div class="mini-projects">{projects.map((p) => <div class="mini-project"><div><span class:list={['project-dot',p.color]}></span><strong>{p.title}</strong><b>{p.percentage}%</b></div><div class="mini-track"><span style={`width:${p.percentage}%`}></span></div><p>{p.category}<span>{p.target} aspiration</span></p></div>)}</div><div class="mini-total"><span>Your support<strong>$22 <small>/ month</small></strong></span><a href="/demo/" class="button">Choose your split →</a></div></div><div class="support-note"><span class="support-note-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span><span><strong>Support is a signal.</strong><small>You still choose your direction.</small></span></div></div>
  </section>
  <div class="principles wrap"><span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span> Your identity, on AT Protocol</span><span><span aria-hidden="true">♡</span> Your community, connected</span><span><span aria-hidden="true">⌂</span> Your page, on your server</span></div>
  <section class="section wrap" id="how-it-works"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Support with a little more meaning</p><h2>More than a tip.<br/>A vote for what comes next.</h2><p>You might be building a sauna, maintaining open-source software, writing essays, or simply making rent. Give each part of your life a place to be supported.</p></div><div class="steps">{[
    ['01','Put your possibilities out there.','Give your projects a story, an optional aspiration, and a home. Ongoing practices belong here just as much as big ideas.'],
    ['02','Let your people tell you what resonates.','Supporters choose one amount and split it between the things they love. Once, monthly, or yearly—whatever feels right.'],
    ['03','Find your direction. Keep your freedom.','See where the encouragement is going. Every tip is yours regardless of a goal; an allocation is a suggestion, not an obligation.'],
  ].map(([number,title,body]) => <article><span class="step-number">{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="freedom-band"><div class="wrap freedom-content"><span class="freedom-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Encouragement, without the strings</p><h2>Your community has a voice.<br/>You have the final say.</h2><p>There’s no all-or-nothing campaign, no funding deadline, and no promise to turn every vote into a task. Support makes more room for your life. The information helps you decide what to do with it.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap" id="demo"><div class="section-heading inline-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Take a look around</p><h2>Your next chapter,<br/>from every angle.</h2></div><p>Explore the actual app screens with fictional creators and sample support. Try the sliders, look through the dashboard, or draft your first project.</p></div><div class="screen-grid">{screens.map(([number,title,body,href,kind]) => <a class="screen-card" href={href}><div class:list={['screen-illustration',kind]} aria-hidden="true">{kind === 'people' ? <div class="avatar-cluster">{[47,44,5,13].map((i)=><img src={`/demo/avatars/${i}.jpg`} alt="" width="52" height="52" loading="lazy"/>)}</div> : kind === 'chart' ? <div class="mini-chart">{[28,44,37,61,53,76,90].map(h=><span style={`height:${h}%`}></span>)}</div> : kind === 'split' ? <div class="split-tiles">{[50,30,20].map(p=><div><b>{p}%</b><span style={`--fill:${p}%`}></span></div>)}</div> : kind === 'story' ? <><img class="story-photo" src="/demo/projects/sauna-small.webp" alt="" width="480" height="320" loading="lazy"/><span class="story-caption">A warm place to gather.</span></> : kind === 'studio' ? <div class="mini-editor"><span>What are you making room for?</span><strong>A neighborhood repair café</strong><span class="editor-publish">Publish project ↗</span></div> : <div class="profile-lines"><img src="/demo/avatars/12.jpg" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy"/><div><b>Alex Rivers</b><span>Making room for good things.</span></div><i></i><i></i></div>}</div><div class="screen-card-copy"><span class="screen-number">{number}</span><h3>{title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>{body}</p></div></a>)}</div></section>
  <section class="network-section wrap"><div class="network-art" aria-hidden="true"><div class="orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="orbit orbit-two"></div><div class="network-center">f</div><img class="orbit-avatar a1" src="/demo/avatars/47.jpg" alt="" width="68" height="68" loading="lazy"/><img class="orbit-avatar a2" src="/demo/avatars/5.jpg" alt="" width="56" height="56" loading="lazy"/><img class="orbit-avatar a3" src="/demo/avatars/44.jpg" alt="" width="60" height="60" loading="lazy"/><img class="orbit-avatar a4" src="/demo/avatars/49.jpg" alt="" width="54" height="54" loading="lazy"/><span class="orbit-label">Good people find good people.</span></div><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A network, not another silo</p><h2>Your own home.<br/>A bigger circle.</h2><p>Sign in with your Bluesky or AT Protocol account. Find creators you already follow, discover friends of friends, and recommend work you believe in.</p><p>Project updates can be Bluesky posts. Public profiles and recommendations live in AT Protocol repositories. Private support records use Habitat’s permissioned storage.</p><a class="text-link" href="/demo/discover/">Meet the demo community →</a></div></section>
  <section class="section setup-section wrap" id="self-host"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Small stack. Your space.</p><h2>Fork it. Make it yours.</h2><p>Feedme is an MIT-licensed TypeScript app built with Astro, Tailwind CSS, and pnpm. Host your own copy on a VPS or a Node host with a persistent disk.</p></div><div class="setup-grid"><ol><li><span>1</span><div><h3>Start with the template</h3><p>Make your own copy of the repo. The source is yours to read, change, and build on.</p></div></li><li><span>2</span><div><h3>Bring your Bluesky handle</h3><p>Use your handle for the creator and admin identity. Your name and avatar can come from your profile.</p></div></li><li><span>3</span><div><h3>Connect. Test. Open your door.</h3><p>Set up HTTPS, private storage, and Stripe Connect. Run the live acceptance checklist before taking payments.</p></div></li></ol><div class="setup-code"><div><span>Start locally</span><span>TypeScript + pnpm</span></div><pre><code>pnpm install
cp .env.example .env
pnpm dev</code></pre><p>Try it without accounts or credentials.<br/>For your live instance:</p><pre><code>BLUESKY_HANDLE=you.bsky.social</code></pre><a href="/get-started/">Read the setup guide →</a></div></div><div class="setup-actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/crs48/feedme/generate">Use the GitHub template ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/crs48/feedme/blob/main/docs/hosting.md">Compare hosting options →</a></div><p class="setup-note">Feedme adds no platform fee. Hosting and payment-provider fees still apply. Live operation needs server configuration and provider credentials, not just a handle.</p></section>
  <section class="faq-section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A few good questions</p><h2>A little clarity.</h2></div><div class="faq-list">{[
    ['Is this crowdfunding?','No. People tip you directly, and support is kept whether or not a project reaches its aspiration. Project allocations help you understand what your community values; they don’t dictate how you spend your resources.'],
    ['Can support be private?','Yes. The app has public, private, and anonymous support choices. Public tips can produce shareable allocation cards. Private and anonymous tips never contribute to public totals. Payment providers and the recipient may still see billing details.'],
    ['Does GitHub Pages handle my payments?','No. This website is a static demo with fictional data. Your own live Feedme uses a Node server for Stripe, OAuth, signed webhooks, and private storage. The public demo never asks for payment details or account credentials.'],
    ['Is it ready for real money?','Feedme is a work in progress. Automated tests and demo flows are covered, but real Stripe Connect, OAuth, and Habitat acceptance checks still need to be completed on a configured instance. Start in test mode, review the setup guide, and treat this as an early release.'],
  ].map(([q,a])=><details><summary>{q}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}</div></section>
  <section class="closing wrap"><p class="eyebrow">A little support. A world of possibility.</p><h2>What would you make<br/>a little more room for?</h2><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/demo/">Try Feedme ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/crs48/feedme">Build it with us</a></div></section>
</Site>
